
# lane/determ — GATE4 A.3 blocker: m1 SSE event-ordering determinism
## WIP 1 — recon verified (both signatures confirmed)
- S1 CONFIRMED: oc-server/src/boot.rs:165 sets `catalog_fetch = true` unconditionally;
  m1 harness spawns the real server binary (tools/parity/src/rust_server.rs spawn_rust,
  env_clear + fresh sandbox → empty KV cache → first refresh pass ALWAYS fetches).
  Box has network (curl models.dev → 200) → fetch succeeds → digest change vs empty
  cache → RefreshOutcome::Updated → `models-dev.refreshed` published at a
  scheduler-dependent time (refresh.rs:253-262; publish ONLY on Updated — verified).
  ALL five goldens contain ZERO `models-dev` frames → any publish = mismatch = S1.
  The golden env was offline (v2 logs-and-ignores offline fetch → no publish).
- S2 CONFIRMED: crates/oc-core/src/session/projector.rs:365-388 — the usage fan-out
  listener (v2 projector.ts:776-787 subscribe → publishSessionUsage → bus.publish
  UsageUpdated at projector.ts:94) fires on session.step.ended/failed/usage.recorded
  but `tokio::spawn`s publish_usage_updated DETACHED (projector.rs:379). The drain
  task then races it to execution.rs:817/:883 terminal publishes (ExecutionHooks::
  settled, execution.rs:808 — the v2 execution.ts:118-147 `settled` equivalent, run
  sequentially after the drain at execution.rs:482). v2's observable order (golden
  prompt_fake_llm group 2): execution.started → usage.updated → execution.succeeded —
  usage fan-out completes before the terminal because the ref's subscriber fiber
  finishes publishSessionUsage inside the drain's yield window. Our detached spawn
  loses that causal edge on a multithreaded runtime → S2 transposition.
- Fix plan: (S1) boot.rs honors OPENCODE_CATALOG_FETCH=0 (rust-test-infra switch,
  production default unchanged — NOT a v2 divergence) + spawn_rust sets it → parity
  boots hermetic. (S2) track per-session in-flight usage fan-outs in the projector;
  ExecutionHooks::settled awaits them before publishing ANY terminal (restores the
  v2 causal chain: durable usage event → project → publish usage.updated ⟶ terminal).
## WIP 2 — fixes implemented, compile clean
- S1: boot.rs now honors OPENCODE_CATALOG_FETCH=0/false/off/no (rust-test-infra
  switch; production default `catalog_fetch = true` unchanged — v2 has no such
  switch, this is harness plumbing, NOT a behavior divergence). spawn_rust
  (tools/parity/src/rust_server.rs) sets OPENCODE_CATALOG_FETCH=0 before
  extra_env so every parity-spawned server boot is hermetic (no models-dev
  fetch loop → no wall-clock-dependent `models-dev.refreshed` publish).
- S2: projector.rs usage fan-out is now (a) SERIAL per session — chained onto
  the previous fan-out like v2's single Stream.runForEach subscription — and
  (b) tracked in-flight via a per-session chain tail (Shared<BoxFuture>) with
  generation-based self-cleanup; new pub wait_usage_fanout(session_id).
  ExecutionHooks::settled (execution.rs, the execution.ts:118-147 equivalent)
  awaits it BEFORE publishing any terminal (succeeded/failed/interrupted) —
  restores the golden order execution.started → usage.updated → terminal.
- cargo check -p oc-core -p oc-server -p parity: clean.
